# clangdev — lift-source

Upstream: https://github.com/conda-forge/clangdev-feedstock
Fork:     https://github.com/NAGAGroup/clangdev-feedstock
Pinned:   28ab51758156090b64f141cb7080164e57dbed08 (conda-forge main, 2026-08-29)

LIFT, NOT SUBMODULE: we do not build this feedstock. Its content is copied
into our own core recipe, because acpp forces LLVM+clang into ONE cmake
configure and conda-forge's per-component split cannot carry it.

THE most valuable lift. WHAT WE LIFT: the nine conda-integration patches this
feedstock has carried for years and our from-scratch recipe never had —
conda gcc detection; linux sysroot detection; CONDA_BUILD_SYSROOT env-var
support; normalizeProgramName dot handling; libclang SOVERSION; PIE default
on macOS; ROCm device library in conda layout; conda mingw paths; versioned
libLTO.dylib ResourceDir. Several map directly onto bugs we hit and worked
around badly.

It is also where the NATIVE clang_impl_<plat> output lives (not in the
activation feedstocks), and it is production proof of two idioms we adopt:
`package_contents: strict: true` and `down_prioritize_variant`.

NOTE: this feedstock ALSO owns clang-tools-extra (see ../clang-tools-extra).

TO DIFF AGAINST UPSTREAM:
    git clone https://github.com/NAGAGroup/clangdev-feedstock
    git -C clangdev-feedstock diff 28ab51758156090b64f141cb7080164e57dbed08..origin/main
